e ""} "Swimming in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1"} "1896 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "3"} "1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "4"} "1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "9"} "1928 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "13"} "1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/SWM'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Swimming at the 2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "9 – 17 August 2008"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/824"} "Beijing Guojia Youyong Zhongxin, Beijing Aolinpike Gongyuan, Beijing"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "At a normal Olympics the stories of the Games may have been the 25 world records broken during the competition or the double victories of " [:a {:href "/athletes/93574"} "Kosuke Kitajima"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/93488"} "Britta Steffen"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/112288"} "Steph Rice"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/115710"} "Becky Adlington"] ". The first champions from Korea and North Africa would also have been more widely feted as would the win of cancer survivor " [:a {:href "/athletes/115922"} "Maarten van der Weijden"] " in the open water swim."] "\n\n" [:p {} "However the story of swimming at the 2008 Beijing Games was the story of one man. " [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Fred Phelps"] " of Baltimore, USA arrived in China as a six-time Olympic champion, with his sights set on five individual and three relay titles from his third Olympic Games. He left undefeated, having broken a plethora of absolute Olympic records. " [:a {:href "/athletes/51572"} "Mark Spitz"] "’s record for most gold medals at a single Games (7 in 1972) fell to Phelps as did the all-time total of Olympic championships held, depending on your view of the official status of the 1906 Olympics, either by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78385"} "Ray Ewry"] " with 10 or shared between Spitz, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78692"} "Carl Lewis"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/29198"} "Larysa Latynina"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/67728"} "Paavo Nurmi"] " with nine apiece. His eight gold medal haul also equalled his own and " [:a {:href "/athletes/31244"} "Aleksandr Dityatin"] "’s shared record of eight medals of any colour at a single Games . Phelps’ performance at Beijing was such that his results would have placed him in the top ten of the overall medal table ahead of such countries as France and Spain. His efforts also earned him a profusion of awards including the Laureus and " [:em {} "Sports Illustrated"] "’s Sportsman of the Year awards for 2008."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Elsewhere 41-year-old " [:a {:href "/athletes/51218"} "Dara Torres"] " returned from retirement to become the oldest female medallist in the history of the sport whilst the oldest world record still standing, the women’s 800 m set by " [:a {:href "/athletes/51014"} "Janet Evans"] " at the Seoul Games of 1988, was finally broken by " [:a {:href "/athletes/115710"} "Becky Adlington"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The major controversy of the year was the introduction of a new generation of so called “super suits”. Woven with polyurethane, spandex and nylon there were claimed to give an aerodynamic advantage of up to 2 % on more traditional materials by more effectively compressing the body and trapping air for buoyancy. Described by some as a form of “technological doping” they were banned from the start of 2009."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Another “star” of the Games was the venue itself. The " [:a {:href "/venues/824"} "Beijing National Aquatics Center"] ", which became popularly known as the " [:em {} "Water Cube"] ", won a succession of architectural awards and was almost universally praised by critics and fans alike.  The design leaned heavily on Chinese symbolism and had a bubble effect on the outer walls which showed to brilliant effect when floodlit."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/261468"} "50 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "14 – 16 August 2008"] "\n" [:td {} "97"]